---------------

The openserverless-operator container image bundles aiohappyeyeballs (2.7.1)
and typing-extensions (4.12.2), which were released under a PSF-2.0 license.
The complete text of the Python Software Foundation License Version 2 is
available at <https://docs.python.org/3/license.html> and is distributed with
each component inside the container image.

---------------

The openserverless-operator container image bundles zip and unzip
((Debian bullseye)), which were released under the Info-ZIP license. The
complete text of the Info-ZIP license is available at
<http://infozip.sourceforge.net/license.html> and is distributed with each
component inside the container image.

---------------

The openserverless-operator container image bundles certifi (2024.12.14),
which was released under an MPL-2.0 license. It is a Category B component:
it is included in binary form only, unmodified and as a separate file. The
complete text of the Mozilla Public License, Version 2.0 is available at
<https://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/> and is distributed with the component inside
the container image. See the WARN file.

---------------

The openserverless-operator container image is built on an upstream base
operating system image, named on the FROM line of the Dockerfile, whose
userland is licensed under mixed licenses including GPL-2.0 and GPL-3.0.
Those operating-system components are supplied by the upstream base image
and are not redistributed by the ASF in source form. See the WARN file.

---------------

The Kubernetes manifests embedded under deploy/ reference third-party
container images (CouchDB, Redis, MongoDB, Kafka, Zookeeper, MinIO,
PostgreSQL, cert-manager, ingress-nginx, Milvus, etcd, FerretDB, SeaweedFS).
Those images are pulled at deployment time by the end user, are NOT
redistributed as part of this product, and their licenses are governed by
their respective publishers.
